{"provider":"jkw-local","version":1,"sourceType":"DOCX","sourcePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user/65d8ea64-e382-5070-81e6-5dde97f8b555/scratchpad/corpus/fn/docx/fn_apa_justified.docx","pdfPath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user/65d8ea64-e382-5070-81e6-5dde97f8b555/scratchpad/corpus/fn/docx/fn_apa_justified.pdf","generatedAt":"2026-11-02T06:35:42.548Z","text":"Introduction\nOsteoarthritis is a degenerative joint condition that leads to the gradual breakdown of articular\ncartilage and remodelling of the underlying bone. The patient described morning stiffness\nlasting less than thirty minutes, which is consistent with a mechanical rather than\ninflammatory process (Brophy & Fillingham, 2022).\nManagement should begin with education and a structured exercise programme, because\nstrengthening the quadriceps reduces pain and improves function for most patients. Weight\nreduction is also recommended when the body mass index exceeds the healthy range, and the\nclinician should revisit these goals at every follow-up visit.\nPharmacological treatment is reserved for symptoms that do not respond to conservative\nmeasures. Topical anti-inflammatory agents are preferred before oral agents in older adults,\nsince gastrointestinal and renal risks increase with age and with concurrent medication use.\nScreening recommendations must be reviewed at the same consultation. According to current\nguidance, adults aged forty-five to seventy-five should be offered colorectal cancer screening,\nand women aged forty to seventy-four should be offered biennial mammography unless a\nhigher-risk pathway applies.\nIn summary, the evidence supports a stepped approach that prioritises non-pharmacological\ncare, reserves medication for persistent symptoms, and integrates preventive screening into\nroutine visits so that the patient's long-term health is protected.\nReferences\nAl Halbusi, Hussam, Al-Sulaiti, Khalid Ibrahim, Alalwan, Ali Abdallah, & Al-Busaidi, Adil S.\n(2025). AI capability and green innovation impact on sustainable performance: Moderating role\nof big data and knowledge management. Technological Forecasting and Social Change, 210,\n123897. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.techfore.2024.123897\nAlshdaifat, Sajead Mowafaq, Aziz, Noor Hidayah Ab, Al Qadi, Fatima, & Alhadab, Yahia. (2024).\nDriving Sustainability Forward: Do Fintech and Digital Transformation Matter? (pp. 223–229).\nSpringer, Singapore. https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-97-2981-4_16\nBag, Surajit. (2024). From resources to sustainability: a practice-based view of net zero economy\nimplementation in small and medium business-to-business firms. Benchmarking, 31 (6), 1876–\n1894. https://doi.org/10.1108/BIJ-01-2023-0056\nBarney, J. (1991). Firm resources and sustained competitive advantage. Journal of Management,\n17 (1), 99–120.\nClarityAI. (2025). Sustainable Finance Regulatory Outlook 2025.\n\nDimaggio, Paul J., & Powell, Walter W. (1983). The Iron Cage Revisited: Institutional\nIsomorphism and Collective Rationality in Organizational Fields. American Sociological Review,\n48 (2), 147–160.\nHair, Joseph F., Risher, Jeffrey J., Sarstedt, Marko, & Ringle, Christian M. (2019). When to use\nand how to report the results of PLS-SEM. In European Business Review (Vol. 31, Issue 1, pp. 2–\n24). Emerald Group Publishing Ltd. https://doi.org/10.1108/EBR-11-2018-0203\nHair, Joseph F., Singh, Sandeep, Kaur, Rajinder, & Dana, Leo Paul. (2022). A Primer on Partial\nLeast Squares Structural Equation Modeling (PLS-SEM). SAGE Publication, 1–352.\nHidayat-ur-Rehman, Imdadullah. (2026). Driving sustainable banking performance: the roles of\ndigital transformation, FinTech adoption, and financial inclusion under regulatory environment\nmoderation. China Finance Review International, ahead-of-print, 1–27.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1108/CFRI-03-2025-0170\nVan der Merwe, Johannes Petrus, de Villiers, Charl, & Maroun, Warren. (2023). This is why\nfirms that are larger are more likely to adopt integrated reporting and what it means for\ninvestors. Journal of Accounting Research, 61 (2), 455–489.\nHenseler, Jörg, Ringle, Christian M., & Sarstedt, Marko. (2015). A new criterion for assessing\ndiscriminant validity in variance-based structural equation modeling. Journal of the Academy of\nMarketing Science, 43 (1), 115–135. https://doi.org/10.1007/s11747-014-0403-8\nWorld Bank Group. (2024). State and Trends of Carbon Pricing 2024. World Bank.\nhttps://openknowledge.worldbank.org/handle/10986/41544","wordCount":523,"characterCount":4073,"pageCount":2,"auditedItems":137,"pages":[{"pageNumber":1,"start":0,"end":2488,"width":612,"height":792,"rotation":0,"itemCount":57,"items":[{"text":"Introduction","start":0,"end":12,"pageNumber":1,"x":90.1,"y":682.65,"width":72.632,"height":14,"transform":[14,0,0,14,90.1,682.65],"fontName":"g_d2_f1","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":"Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint condition that leads to the gradual breakdown of articular","start":13,"end":110,"pageNumber":1,"x":90.1,"y":666.45,"width":431.13399999999984,"height":11,"transform":[11,0,0,11,90.1,666.45],"fontName":"g_d2_f2","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":"cartilage and remodelling of the underlying bone. The patient described morning stiffness","start":111,"end":200,"pageNumber":1,"x":90.1,"y":651.95,"width":431.34299999999985,"height":11,"transform":[11,0,0,11,90.1,651.95],"fontName":"g_d2_f2","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":"lasting","start":201,"end":208,"pageNumber":1,"x":90.1,"y":637.45,"width":30.272,"height":11,"transform":[11,0,0,11,90.1,637.45],"fontName":"g_d2_f2","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":" ","start":208,"end":209,"pageNumber":1,"x":120.37199999999999,"y":637.45,"width":7.589999999999989,"height":0,"transform":[11,0,0,11,120.37199999999999,637.45],"fontName":"g_d2_f2","direction":"ltr","hasEOL":false},{"text":"less","start":209,"end":213,"pageNumber":1,"x":127.96199999999997,"y":637.45,"width":16.455999999999996,"height":11,"transform":[11,0,0,11,